# Who must review what.
#
# The CI workflow is the gate that runs the build, the pending-migration check and the concurrency
# suite against a real SQL Server - and the step that fails the run when any test skipped, because
# a skipped concurrency test reports green while proving nothing. An unreviewed edit to that file
# can quietly turn the whole check into theatre, so it needs a named owner rather than an ordinary
# diff review.
#
# Pair this with branch protection: Settings -> Branches -> master -> Require review from Code
# Owners, alongside Require status checks (build-and-test). CODEOWNERS alone is advisory.
/.github/           @grigoravagyann
/Directory.Build.props  @grigoravagyann
/global.json        @grigoravagyann
/.config/           @grigoravagyann

# The two security boundaries this system rests on: a staff token for branch A must not act on
# branch B, and a participant token for tab A must not act on tab B.
/src/Yalla.Api/Authorization/       @grigoravagyann
/src/Yalla.Infrastructure/Identity/ @grigoravagyann
